  "question": "Is science getting faster—or merely producing more?",
  "verdict": {
    "label": "More capacity and output; selective acceleration; no system-wide speed verdict",
    "text": "Measured R&D intensity and publication volume have risen globally, and AlphaFold demonstrates a large capability jump in one research task. Those observations do not establish that reliable discoveries or clinical translation are accelerating across science.",
    "direction": "Inputs and volume are rising. Reliability and translation move on separate clocks.",
    "distribution": "R&D intensity and article output remain uneven across countries and fields.",
    "confidence": "Conditional"
  },
  "questions": [
    "Where are we now?",
    "What direction are we moving?",
    "Who is benefiting or carrying the cost?",
    "What are the competing explanations?",
    "What evidence would change our current conclusion?"
